<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2025-09-15T06:34:15+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Mon, 15 Sep 2025 06:34:15 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title>‘Up to China’: Donald Trump leaves TikTok’s US ban in doubt; hints at a factor that could save app</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123889597.cms" /&gt;President Trump expressed uncertainty regarding TikTok's future in the US, hinting that China's decision would be pivotal ahead of the looming September 17 deadline. Despite national security concerns and pressure from lawmakers, Trump acknowledged TikTok's role in connecting with younger voters during his campaign. With negotiations ongoing and previous deadlines extended, another extension seems probable, leaving the platform's fate unresolved.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/up-to-china-donald-trump-leaves-tiktoks-us-ban-in-doubt-hints-at-a-factor-that-could-save-app/articleshow/123889597.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/up-to-china-donald-trump-leaves-tiktoks-us-ban-in-doubt-hints-at-a-factor-that-could-save-app/articleshow/123889597.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-15T06:23:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123889672,imgsize-740641.cms"/></item><item><title>Charlie Kirk assassination: 'Non-cooperative' Tyler Robinson under special watch; governor says he 'has not confessed' yet</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123889505.cms" /&gt;Tyler Robinson, accused of assassinating Charlie Kirk at a Utah Valley University event, is under special watch for a mental health evaluation. Following a 33-hour manhunt, Robinson was apprehended after his father recognised him in FBI footage and intervened due to suicidal concerns. Governor Brian Cox stated Robinson isn't cooperating, but his family and partner are assisting investigators, noting his deep leftist indoctrination.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/charlie-kirk-assassination-non-cooperative-tyler-robinson-under-special-watch-governor-says-he-has-not-confessed-yet/articleshow/123889505.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/charlie-kirk-assassination-non-cooperative-tyler-robinson-under-special-watch-governor-says-he-has-not-confessed-yet/articleshow/123889505.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-15T05:56:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123889554,imgsize-624098.cms"/></item><item><title>Jim Edgar passes: Former Illinois governor dies at 79 from pancreatic cancer; diagnosed earlier this year</title><description